  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $25{y}^{2}-9{x}^{2}=225.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{y}^{2}-9{x}^{2} & =225 \\\\ 25{y}^{2}-9(0)^{2} & =225 \\\\ 25{y}^{2} & =225 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ y & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 3).$",
